Vorstehers des Hochbaudepartements wird die Baudirektion ersucht, die Planungszone\nim Sinne von § 346 Abs. 3 PBG um zwei Jahre zu verlängern.\nInzwischen hat der Stadtrat von Zürich mit Weisung vom 18. September 2013 die Teil-\nrevision der Bau- und Zonenordnung zur Anhörung und öffentlichen Auflage verabschie\ndet. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAPN 3-design conjecture for two quartic-dependent exponents | MathDB (https://mathdb.com/p/342382/apn-3-design-conjecture-for-two-quartic-dependent-exponents)\nciteturn2search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; # APN 3-design conjecture for two quartic-dependent exponents ... Chunming Tang, “Infinite families of 3-designs from APN functions”, arXiv:1904.04071 (2019). ... Refresh searches the literature and the public web for attempts on this problem, and writes the first summary here.\n\n# APN 3-design conjecture for two quartic-dependent exponents\n\n7 years old · traced to 2019\n\nLet $q=2^n$q=2 n, with $n\\geq5$n≥5 odd, and let $B_s$B s​ be the associated base block. Two-exponent APN 3-design conjecture. The incidence structure\n\n$$\\mathbb{AP}_{n,s}=\\left(\\operatorname{GF}(q),\\operatorname{GA}_1(q)(B_s)\\right)$$AP n,s​=(GF(q),GA 1​(q)(B s​))\n\nis a $3$3-$\\left(q,\\frac q2,\\frac{q(q-4)}8\\right)$(q,2 q​,8 q(q−4)​) design in either of the following cases: $s=2^{(n-1)/2}+2^{(n-1)/4}-1$s=2(n−1)/2+2(n−1)/4−1 when $n\\equiv1\\pmod4$n≡1(mod 4), or $s=2^{(n-1)/2}+2^{(3n-1)/4}-1$s=2(n−1)/2+2(3 n−1)/4−1 when $n\\equiv3\\pmod4$n≡3(mod 4). These cases were included among conjectures computationally confirmed for $n\\in\\{5,7\\}$n∈{5,7}; the general statement remains open.\n\nReferences\n\n  1. Chunming Tang, “Infinite families of 3-designs from APN functions”, arXiv:1904.04071 (2019).\n\napn-functionsdesign-theoryfinite-fields\n\n## Progress summary\n\nRefresh Never refreshed\n\nNothing recorded yet. Refresh searches the literature and the public web for attempts on th